Hi,

I was facing incompatibility between the packages Leaflet and NVD3, to make them work together the only way is to change the codes inside nv.d3.css file in the library of rchart installed into my computer to:

svg{
  -webkit-touch-callout: none;
  -webkit-user-select: none;
  -khtml-user-select: none;

-moz-user-select: none;
  -ms-user-select: none;
  user-select: none;

 /* Trying to get SVG to act like a greedy block in all browsers */
  display: block;
/*
  width:100%;
  height:100%;
}*/}

Locally it works perfectly but when I publish it using SHINY.IO <http://SHINY.IO> it doesn´t work. How do I make it work in Shiny.io too?

Please help.

Best Regards

If you want to include custom css with your application, you'll have to include your own css file:

Checkout this article:

http://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/css.html

